  "hook": "Headquarters of the Maltese Club of San Francisco from 1930, now a church.",
  "historical_record": [
    {
      "date": "1930",
      "kind": "community use",
      "description": "The Maltese Club of San Francisco opened its headquarters here under the directorship of Francis Grech; the crowd at the opening was so large that people had to be turned away. The club kept a Maltese band and a theatrical group that performed in Maltese, and did philanthropic work. Its enrolled membership passed 750 by 1935. The building, heavily altered, is now Saint Paul Tabernacle Baptist Church.",
